        "abstract": "This paper proposes a wireless receiver RF Power Detector (PD) for 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz WLAN bands with innovative offset compensation and measurement method, designed in 65 nm CMOS technology. The PD is based on two Common Source Pairs (CSP), the first performs true RMS conversion and the second identical CSP cancels the DC component. The PD has two modes of operation. The first is the offset compensation mode which is active during the transmitting phase. The second is the measurement mode which is active during the receiving phase. In this mode, PD measures the RMS value of the input RF signal and converts it to 8-bit digital word. The designed PD measures powers in the range from -30 dBm to -2 dBm with a resolution of 1dB with a maximum measurement time of 640 ns.",
